{"id":"2026-10-24-markets-procter-and-gamble-shares","date":"2026-10-24","topic":"markets","region":"americas","headline":"Procter and Gamble Shares Rise After Strong Quarterly Earnings","source":{"name":"CNBC","url":"https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/22/procter-gamble-pg-q1-2027-earnings.html"},"accent":"ca","tiers":{"t1":{"sentences":[{"text":"Procter and Gamble made a lot of money recently.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"The company sold many home items to many people.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","O","O","O","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Its stock price went up after the good news.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","V","V","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Many shoppers bought cleaning items every single day.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","O","O","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"The big firm earned more money over three months.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","V","O","O","M","M","M"],"dur":null}],"bands":{"core1000":93,"core1800":0,"ngsl":0,"tsl":2,"nawl":0,"beyond":5},"grammar":[{"i":2,"focus":"went up","title":"Phrasal Verbs","note":"A phrasal verb combines a main verb with a particle like 'up' to create a distinct meaning. Here, 'went up' means 'increased' or 'rose' in value."},{"i":4,"focus":"more money","title":"Comparative Quantifiers","note":"The word 'more' is used before the uncountable noun 'money' to show a greater quantity. It compares the firm's current earnings to past periods."}]},"t2":{"sentences":[{"text":"Procter and Gamble reported higher sales because people bought home items.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","V","O","O","M","S","V","O","O"],"dur":null},{"text":"Company stock prices jumped five percent because total profit was very strong.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","V","M","M","M","S","S","V","C","C"],"dur":null},{"text":"Total product sales grew as people bought more soap and detergent.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","V","M","S","V","O","O","O","O"],"dur":null},{"text":"Wealthy buyers bought costly items but poor buyers saved their money.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","O","O","M","S","S","V","O","O"],"dur":null},{"text":"The company will raise its future sales plan for all its investors.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","V","O","O","O","O","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"The business will continue to sell goods to different types of shoppers.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","V","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null}],"bands":{"core1000":83,"core1800":3,"ngsl":4,"tsl":6,"nawl":0,"beyond":4},"grammar":[{"i":0,"focus":"because","title":"Subordinating Conjunctions of Cause","note":"The conjunction 'because' introduces a clause that explains the reason for the main action. It tells us why Procter and Gamble reported higher sales."},{"i":4,"focus":"will raise","title":"Simple Future Tense","note":"The modal auxiliary 'will' pairs with the base verb 'raise' to express a future action. It indicates a decision or projection about company plans."}]},"t3":{"sentences":[{"text":"Consumer goods giant Procter & Gamble has beaten Wall Street profit expectations this quarter.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","S","S","V","V","O","O","O","O","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Shares rose over 5% after the company reported adjusted earnings of $2.00 per share.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","M","M","M","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O"],"dur":null},{"text":"Total sales volume, which measures actual product quantities sold, increased by 2.4% recently.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","V","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Strong demand for cleaning products helped the fabric and home care division grow 4.3%.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O","C","C"],"dur":null},{"text":"Executive Andre Schulten noted that high-income consumers still buy more expensive new products.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","V","M","S","S","M","V","O","O","O","O"],"dur":null},{"text":"In contrast, low-income households are stretching their budgets to cover higher living costs.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","S","S","V","V","O","O","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"P&G raised its sales guidance, which is an official company forecast for future growth.","voice":null,"roles":["S","V","O","O","O","S","V","C","C","C","C","C","C","C"],"dur":null}],"bands":{"core1000":76,"core1800":15,"ngsl":5,"tsl":4,"nawl":0,"beyond":0},"grammar":[{"i":0,"focus":"has beaten","title":"Present Perfect Tense","note":"The present perfect uses 'has' plus the past participle 'beaten' to link a past event to the present. It highlights the current relevance of the recent quarterly performance."},{"i":2,"focus":"which measures actual product quantities sold","title":"Non-defining Relative Clauses","note":"This clause gives extra, parenthetical information about 'Total sales volume'. It is separated by commas and begins with the relative pronoun 'which'."}]},"t4":{"sentences":[{"text":"Shares of Procter & Gamble surged over 5% after quarterly results exceeded Wall Street analyst estimates.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","S","V","M","M","M","S","S","V","O","O","O","O"],"dur":null},{"text":"Adjusted earnings reached $2.00 per share, while total net income dropped slightly to $4.73 billion.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","O","O","O","M","S","S","S","V","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Revenue growth was supported by a 2.4% overall increase in product sales volume across divisions.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"The fabric and home care segment led performance, with volume rising 4.3% on strong detergent demand.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","S","S","V","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Conversely, healthcare volume fell 2.9% because consumer demand for oral care items like toothpaste declined.","voice":null,"roles":["M","S","S","V","M","M","S","S","S","S","S","S","S","S","V"],"dur":null},{"text":"Chief Financial Officer Andre Schulten stated that economic conditions remain split between different consumer income levels.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","S","V","M","S","S","V","C","C","C","C","C","C"],"dur":null},{"text":"Following the acquisition of supplements brand Thorne, full-year sales growth guidance was raised up to 4%.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","M","M","M","M","S","S","S","S","V","V","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Chief Executive Officer Shailesh Jejurikar confirmed that full-year earnings expectations remain on track despite market challenges.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","S","V","M","S","S","S","V","C","C","M","M","M"],"dur":null}],"bands":{"core1000":68,"core1800":15,"ngsl":7,"tsl":4,"nawl":1,"beyond":5},"grammar":[{"i":2,"focus":"was supported","title":"Passive Voice","note":"The passive form 'was supported' shifts the focus to the subject 'Revenue growth'. It emphasizes the condition being acted upon rather than the cause directly."},{"i":3,"focus":"with volume rising 4.3%","title":"With-Prepositional Absolute Clause","note":"This structure uses 'with' followed by a noun and a present participle to add supporting context. It concisely explains how or why the segment led performance."}]},"t5":{"sentences":[{"text":"Consumer goods titan Procter & Gamble saw its stock rally by over 5% after delivering fiscal first-quarter earnings that surpassed Wall Street projections.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","S","V","O","O","O"],"dur":null},{"text":"The company posted adjusted earnings of $2.00 per share, while net income dipped slightly to $4.73 billion from $4.75 billion a year earlier.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O","M","S","S","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Underlying demand displayed resilience as overall product volume expanded by 2.4%, marking a solid start to the company's fiscal year.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","V","O","M","S","S","S","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Outperforming other segments, the fabric and home care division logged a 4.3% volume gain, propelled by steady consumer purchases of laundry detergents.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","S","S","S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"In contrast, the healthcare division lagged behind with a 2.9% volume drop, reflecting softer demand for personal care products like toothpaste.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","S","S","S","V","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Addressing analysts, Chief Financial Officer Andre Schulten described a bifurcated economic backdrop where affluent shoppers trade up while lower-income households stretch tight budgets.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","S","S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","M","S","S","V","M","M","S","S","V","O","O"],"dur":null},{"text":"Chief Executive Officer Shailesh Jejurikar reaffirmed core per-share earnings guidance of $6.89 to $7.11 despite ongoing macroeconomic uncertainties.","voice":null,"roles":["S","S","S","S","S","V","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","O","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null},{"text":"Bolstered by the recent acquisition of supplements brand Thorne, management raised its full-year sales growth forecast upward to a range of 2% to 4%.","voice":null,"roles":["M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","S","V","O","O","O","O","O","M","M","M","M","M","M","M","M"],"dur":null}],"bands":{"core1000":57,"core1800":14,"ngsl":9,"tsl":7,"nawl":1,"beyond":12},"grammar":[{"i":3,"focus":"Outperforming other segments","title":"Fronted Participle Modifiers","note":"This present participle phrase acts as an introductory adverbial modifier for the main clause. It describes an ongoing characteristic of the subject 'the fabric and home care division'."},{"i":5,"focus":"where affluent shoppers trade up","title":"Relative Adverbs in Complex Sentences","note":"The relative adverb 'where' modifies the abstract noun 'backdrop' to introduce a descriptive clause. It establishes the economic context in which consumer behaviors are compared."}]}},"glossary":[{"word":"profit","lemma":"profit","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈprɑːfɪt/","definition":"Money earned by a business after all costs are paid.","tiers":["t2","t3"]},{"word":"investors","lemma":"investor","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɪnˈvɛstərz/","definition":"People or firms that put money into businesses for profit.","tiers":["t2"]},{"word":"earnings","lemma":"earnings","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɜːrnɪŋz/","definition":"The total profit that a business generates during a period.","tiers":["t3","t4","t5"]},{"word":"guidance","lemma":"guidance","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɡaɪdəns/","definition":"A business forecast about future sales or earnings performance.","tiers":["t3","t4","t5"]},{"word":"acquisition","lemma":"acquisition","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌækwɪˈzɪʃən/","definition":"The act of buying another company to expand operations.","tiers":["t4","t5"]},{"word":"bifurcated","lemma":"bifurcate","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈbaɪfərˌkeɪtɪd/","definition":"Divided into two distinct or contrasting parts.","tiers":["t5"]},{"word":"resilience","lemma":"resilience","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rɪˈzɪliəns/","definition":"The ability to stay strong during difficult economic periods.","tiers":["t5"]}],"words":{"procter":{"l":"Procter","p":"name","i":"/ˈprɑːktər/","d":"surname part of the company name Procter & Gamble","b":"beyond","img":null},"and":{"l":"and","p":"conj","i":"/ænd/","d":"used to connect words or clauses","b":"core1000","img":null},"gamble":{"l":"Gamble","p":"name","i":"/ˈɡæmbəl/","d":"surname part of the company name Procter & Gamble","b":"beyond","img":null},"made":{"l":"make","p":"verb","i":"/meɪd/","d":"earned or produced money","b":"core1000","img":"art/stock/words/make.jpg"},"a":{"l":"a","p":"det","i":"/ə/","d":"used before a no